---

3. There is no MachineConfig degradation

These are good:

RenderDegraded: False
NodeDegraded:   False
Degraded:       False

So MCO itself is healthy.


---

4. Why CRI-O may still not start

In your previous messages, CRI-O was failing.

Since the MCP is paused, even if you fix or create a new MachineConfig, it will never be applied until the pool is unpaused.

However, pausing the MCP does not itself stop CRI-O. A CRI-O startup failure is usually due to an invalid configuration (for example, a bad CRI-O drop-in, runtime configuration, or network setting).


