One thing caught my attention

Your MCP has the annotation:

sriovnetwork.openshift.io/state: Paused

This suggests that the SR-IOV Operator may have intentionally paused the MachineConfigPool while applying configuration. If that operation never completed, the pool can remain paused.

Could you also share the outputs of these commands?

oc get nodes
oc get mcp
oc describe node sno1
journalctl -xeu crio.service

These will help determine whether the problem is the node becoming NotReady, the paused MCP, or the underlying CRI-O configuration error.
